      "id": "TASK-1",
      "title": "W1: cut a wave from an index snapshot when changes are staged",
      "action": "In setup, when the index differs from HEAD, write the index as a tree and cut the lanes from `git commit-tree <tree> -p HEAD` (fixed parallel2 identity), so staged earlier-wave work is in the lanes' base without a commit on the target. Record `head_sha` (HEAD at setup) beside `base_sha`; `moved_note` compares HEAD with `head_sha` (falling back to `base_sha` for older state). Setup refuses only unstaged or untracked paths inside lane files; staged paths go into the snapshot, and the note counts unstaged or untracked paths and says to stage them. Print `note: lanes cut from an index snapshot <base7> of HEAD <head7> (<n> staged paths)`. At stage, a changed path is refused when it is unstaged or untracked in the checkout, or staged with index content that differs from the lane base.",
